      "name": "any_comment_concrete_personal_anecdote",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "OC_comments"
      ],
      "definition": "Counter-argument comments (OC_comments, not the OP): 1 if any comment employs a concrete personal anecdote, else 0.",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read the OC_comments JSON list (comments by users other than the OP; ignore conversation and later replies). Return 1 if at least one comment uses a concrete personal anecdote, i.e. the commenter recounts a specific experience of their own or someone they personally know (particular events, people, or situations) as part of their counter-argument. Quoted text from others, hypotheticals, generic statistics and general claims do not count. Return 0 if the list is valid and no comment does. Return null if OC_comments is missing or malformed. Empty valid list gives 0."
